    "title": "New \"Free Little Food Pantry\" unveiled in Newburgh - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nNEWBURGH, Ind. (WEHT) — The fight against food insecurity continues in the Tri-State with a new food pantry being unveiled in Newburgh.\nThe pantry, titled Free Little Food Pantry, was donated by a girl scout troop as the final project of their community service journey on Wednesday. The troop partnered with the town council to install the pantry at Aurand Trailhead in Newburgh.\nOfficials say it’s an accessible, stigma-free resource to help neighbors facing food insecurity.\n“We wanted to help food insecurity in our area, and we found one of the best ways to do that is donating non-perishables, and there was a need for one in this area,” says former Girl Scout Lizzie Adamnission. “We found this was the best area. So we hope that people can be able to get food from this.”\nThose in the area are encouraged to bring non-perishable food items to help stock the pantry.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
